  "preamble": "Loanword adaptation of the voiced postalveolar affricate [dʒ] as the voiced alveolo-palatal affricate [dʑ]. Japanese lacks postalveolar sibilants, so English /dʒ/ is borrowed with the kana ジ/ジャ/ジュ/ジョ, whose consonant is pronounced [dʑ] word-initially (alternating with [ʑ] between vowels).",
